{"parentUuid":"f1b55797-8978-47ab-844d-5c04b41beef7","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aaa9a46efbbbe9596","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01TSCcmFhdEHKwQusqVfELvi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KLLAvCQcMccWXHDYT8Kvgd","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"DeepMind AlphaProof 2025 2026 successor extensions optimization"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21280,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":353,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":21280},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":353,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21280,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":21280,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaowzjesMRhkAtRiCAJdr","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"5bda2ed0-9625-4010-abb6-4d78cd63cd29","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:51:41.726Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f1b55797-8978-47ab-844d-5c04b41beef7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"aaa9a46efbbbe9596","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BNL1QHpJYXHg9YdzfqtgrB","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"VeriPB CakePB pseudo-boolean proof certificate CP-SAT verified 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Documentation of VeriPB and CakePB for the SAT Competition 2025 Markus Anders\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/downloads/checkers/veripb.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"VERIPB and CAKEPB in the SAT Competition 2023\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2024/downloads/checkers/veripb.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Documentation of VeriPB and CakePB for the SAT Competition 2023 Bart Bogaerts\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2023/downloads/proposals/veripb.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Practically Feasible Proof Logging for Pseudo-Boolean Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.21\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - StephanGocht/VeriPB: Verifier for pseudo-Boolean proofs · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/StephanGocht/VeriPB\"},{\"title\":\"PB25 Pseudo-Boolean Competition 2025 organized by Olivier Roussel,\",\"url\":\"https://www.cril.univ-artois.fr/PB25/slides/PB25.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"PBLean: Pseudo-Boolean Proof Certificates for Lean 4\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2602.08692\"},{\"title\":\"Practically Feasible Proof Logging for Pseudo-Boolean Optimization - Andy Oertel\",\"url\":\"https://aoertel.de/publications/2025-practically-feasible-proof-logging-for-pb/\"},{\"title\":\"MIAO / Software / VeriPB · GitLab\",\"url\":\"https://gitlab.com/MIAOresearch/software/VeriPB\"},{\"title\":\"Formal Methods in Computer-Aided Design 2024 Translating Pseudo-Boolean Proofs\",\"url\":\"https://repositum.tuwien.at/bitstream/20.500.12708/200790/1/Nukala-2024-Translating%20Pseudo-Boolean%20Proofs%20into%20Boolean%20Clausal%20Proofs-vor.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found relevant information about VeriPB and CakePB:\n\n## Overview\n\nVeriPB is a proof checker that accepts proofs in an \"augmented\" proof format with a rich collection of rules for proof logging, while CakePB is a formally verified proof checker that supports a \"kernel\" subset of commands, with VeriPB serving as a preprocessor to compile augmented proofs into kernel format for formal verification by CakePB.\n\n## Pseudo-Boolean Proof Format\n\nThe pseudo-Boolean proof format used for VeriPB supports proof logging for decision, enumeration, and optimization problems, as well as problem reformulations, all in a unified format.\n\n## 2025 Applications\n\nIn the SAT competition 2025, the only supported option is to run both VeriPB and CakePB together. Additionally, an efficient toolchain based on VeriPB and CakePB has been developed for formally verified pseudo-Boolean optimization, and proof logging has been implemented for the full range of techniques in state-of-the-art solvers RoundingSat and Sat4j, including core-guided search and linear programming.\n\nRegarding CP-SAT specifically: While the search results mention that VeriPB is a proof checker for verifying pseudo-Boolean certificates of satisfiability, unsatisfiability, and optimality bounds, there is no specific information about CP-SAT integration in the retrieved results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c3fd152d-2623-4d3f-bbbe-c1530e309ad2","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:51:48.519Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f1b55797-8978-47ab-844d-5c04b41beef7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"59c36918-5078-432d-82fa-a1029052c68b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"aaa9a46efbbbe9596","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017nc9af3qyYBLUiK8YkPj46","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"AlphaProof Lean 4 combinatorial optimization NP-hard optimality proof 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"AlphaProof Paper\",\"url\":\"https://www.julian.ac/blog/2025/11/13/alphaproof-paper/\"},{\"title\":\"AI achieves silver-medal standard solving International Mathematical Olympiad problems — Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/blog/ai-solves-imo-problems-at-silver-medal-level/\"},{\"title\":\"Major Breakthroughs in Lean 4-Based Auto-Formalized Mathematics\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.virginia.edu/~rmw7my/Courses/AgenticAISpring2026/Major%20Breakthroughs%20in%20Lean%204-Based%20Auto-Formalized%20Mathematics.html\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaProof: AI for Formal Mathematics\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/alphaproof\"},{\"title\":\"Olympiad-level formal mathematical reasoning with reinforcement learning - PubMed\",\"url\":\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41225005/\"},{\"title\":\"Mathematicians put AlphaProof to the test\",\"url\":\"https://media.nature.com/original/magazine-assets/d41586-025-03585-5/d41586-025-03585-5.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Olympiad-level formal mathematical reasoning with reinforcement learning | Nature\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-09833-y\"},{\"title\":\"Lean Programming Language\",\"url\":\"https://lean-lang.org/\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaProof and the IMO - by Greg Burnham - Lemmata\",\"url\":\"https://lemmata.substack.com/p/alphaproof-and-the-imo\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google-deepmind/formal-conjectures: A collection of formalized statements of conjectures in Lean. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/formal-conjectures\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding AlphaProof and Lean 4:\n\n## AlphaProof Overview\n\nAlphaProof is an AlphaZero-inspired agent that learns to find formal proofs through reinforcement learning by training on millions of auto-formalized problems, and for the most difficult problems, it uses test-time RL, a method of generating and learning from millions of related problem variants at inference time to enable deep, problem-specific adaptation.\n\n## Performance and Capabilities\n\nAlphaProof is a new reinforcement-learning based system for formal math reasoning that, together with AlphaGeometry 2, solved four out of six problems from the 2024 International Mathematical Olympiad, achieving the same level as a silver medalist in the competition for the first time.\n\nWith test-time RL, AlphaProof reached particularly strong performance in number theory (75.7%) and algebra (72.6%), and also made progress in combinatorics (20.3%).\n\n## Combinatorics and NP-Hard Problems\n\nRegarding your specific query about combinatorial optimization and NP-hard optimality proofs: The search results mention that two combinatorics problems remained unsolved in the 2024 IMO competition. However, the search results do not contain specific information about AlphaProof proving optimality for NP-hard combinatorial optimization problems or attempting to resolve NP-hardness questions in 2025.\n\nThe results focus primarily on AlphaProof's performance on IMO problems and formal mathematics verification in Lean 4, rather than on algorithmic complexity theory or NP-hardness proofs specifically.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"99db86e9-5893-4596-8911-5f74a6ca24b3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:51:48.524Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"59c36918-5078-432d-82fa-a1029052c68b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"5bda2ed0-9625-4010-abb6-4d78cd63cd29","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"aaa9a46efbbbe9596","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KLLAvCQcMccWXHDYT8Kvgd","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"DeepMind AlphaProof 2025 2026 successor extensions optimization\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Olympiad-level formal mathematical reasoning with reinforcement learning | Nature\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-09833-y\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced version of Gemini with Deep Think officially achieves gold-medal standard at the International Mathematical Olympiad — Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/blog/advanced-version-of-gemini-with-deep-think-officially-achieves-gold-medal-standard-at-the-international-mathematical-olympiad/\"},{\"title\":\"AI achieves silver-medal standard solving International Mathematical Olympiad problems — Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/blog/ai-solves-imo-problems-at-silver-medal-level/\"},{\"title\":\"Demis Hassabis AGI Roadmap: Gemini, AlphaFold & DeepMind Strategy\",\"url\":\"https://www.useluminix.com/reports/market-research/understanding-demis-hassabis-s-agi-roadmap-gemini-alphafold-and-deepmind-s-bet\"},{\"title\":\"Google DeepMind - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Google_DeepMind\"},{\"title\":\"[Research Press Release] Artificial intelligence: A mathematics medal-worthy AI system (Nature) | Nature Portfolio\",\"url\":\"https://www.natureasia.com/en/info/press-releases/detail/9147\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaProof Paper\",\"url\":\"https://www.julian.ac/blog/2025/11/13/alphaproof-paper/\"},{\"title\":\"DeepMind claims its AI performs better than International Mathematical Olympiad gold medalists | TechCrunch\",\"url\":\"https://techcrunch.com/2025/02/07/deepmind-claims-its-ai-performs-better-than-international-mathematical-olympiad-gold-medalists/\"},{\"title\":\"Google DeepMind and Google.org announce AI for Math Initiative\",\"url\":\"https://blog.google/technology/google-deepmind/ai-for-math/\"},{\"title\":\"Olympiad-level formal mathematical reasoning with reinforcement learning - PubMed\",\"url\":\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41225005/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about DeepMind AlphaProof and its recent developments:\n\n## AlphaProof 2024-2025 Performance\n\nAlphaProof achieved Olympiad-level formal mathematical reasoning, with performance reaching a score equivalent to that of a silver medallist at the 2024 International Mathematical Olympiad competition. AlphaProof solved two algebra problems and one number theory problem, including the hardest problem in the competition, solved by only five contestants at that year's IMO.\n\n## Architecture and Optimization\n\nBy combining an AlphaZero-inspired learning framework with a curriculum of millions of auto-formalized problems and a TTRL approach based on variant generation, AlphaProof has demonstrated a powerful capacity for automated mathematical reasoning. The proof network is continually improved using experience from both successful proof and disproof attempts, refining its policy to predict effective tactics and adjusting its value to estimate the expected return.\n\n## Future Extensions\n\nResearchers still have many ideas for how they can make AlphaProof better as well as more general, now that they have shown that the principles of RL with search work just as well for LLMs. Additionally, agents that combine natural language fluency with rigorous reasoning—including verified reasoning in formal languages—will become invaluable tools for mathematicians, scientists, engineers, and researchers.\n\n## 2026 Context\n\nWhile recent approaches were based purely on natural language with Gemini, DeepMind continues making progress on formal systems, AlphaGeometry and AlphaProof.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"805d22a1-8270-4bee-a430-4521bd9ecec7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:51:49.718Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5bda2ed0-9625-4010-abb6-4d78cd63cd29","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c4b69c0f-63ca-40c7-a4e2-8740b1548db0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"aaa9a46efbbbe9596","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HNvmvmPnUaC4YgvPWbcLqt","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Lean 4 mathlib SAT solver formalization verified pseudo-boolean\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"PBLean: Pseudo-Boolean Proof Certificates for Lean 4\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2602.08692v1\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - leanprover/leansat: This package provides an interface and foundation for verified SAT reasoning · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/leanprover/leansat\"},{\"title\":\"SATurn : SAT Solver-prover in lean 4\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/siddhartha-gadgil/Saturn\"},{\"title\":\"Lean Programming Language\",\"url\":\"https://lean-lang.org/\"},{\"title\":\"SATurn : SAT Solver-prover in lean 4\",\"url\":\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/archive/stream/270676-lean4/topic/Lean.204.20SAT.20Solver-Prover.html\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Solver-Prover in Lean 4 · Artificial Intelligence and Mathematics\",\"url\":\"https://siddhartha-gadgil.github.io/automating-mathematics/posts/sat-prover-lean/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - leanprover-community/mathlib4: The math library of Lean 4 · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4\"},{\"title\":\"Verifying SAT Encodings in Lean Cayden Codel CMU-CS-22-106 May 6, 2022\",\"url\":\"http://reports-archive.adm.cs.cmu.edu/anon/2022/CMU-CS-22-106.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Mathlib: A Foundation for Formal Mathematics Research and Verification — Lean Lang\",\"url\":\"https://lean-lang.org/use-cases/mathlib/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - lean-dojo/LeanMillenniumPrizeProblems: Formalization of the Millennium Problems in Lean 4 · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/lean-dojo/LeanMillenniumPrizeProblems\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here are the key findings related to your query about Lean 4, mathlib, SAT solver formalization, and pseudo-boolean reasoning:\n\n## PBLean: Pseudo-Boolean Proof Certificates\n\nThe most directly relevant result is PBLean, a method for importing VeriPB pseudo-Boolean (PB) proof certificates into Lean 4. This represents a significant development in verified constraint solving:\n\n- The approach uses reflection: a Boolean checker function whose soundness is fully proved in Lean and executed as compiled native code\n- The method scales to proofs with tens of thousands of steps that would exhaust memory under explicit proof-term construction\n- The checker supports all VeriPB kernel rules, including cutting-plane derivations and proof-by-contradiction subproofs\n\nPBLean supports verified encodings to derive theorems about the original combinatorial problems rather than about PB constraints alone, closing the trust gap between solver output and problem semantics since the constraint translation and its correctness proof are both formalized in Lean.\n\n## Related SAT Solver Verification Work\n\nThe LeanSAT package is meant to provide an interface and foundation for verified SAT reasoning, offering SAT tactics for automatically discharging goals about boolean expressions using a SAT solver. Additionally, it includes a verified LRAT certificate checker used to import UNSAT proofs generated by high performance SAT solvers like CaDiCal.\n\nOther relevant Lean 4 projects include SATurn, a SAT solver-prover in lean 4 based on the DPLL algorithm that, given a SAT problem, produces either a solution or a resolution tree showing why there is no solution.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b7b8c5be-d683-43ca-8d85-2a13a0f95821","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:51:50.523Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c4b69c0f-63ca-40c7-a4e2-8740b1548db0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","vers