{"parentUuid":"58537d00-ea71-4030-9969-a67161f76e29","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aaa9a46efbbbe9596","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01QLPaKCZ1PcvoSkbnjRsvPK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JbMc9WXc9rTrgHgLenE4J8","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"Lean 4 grid placement combinatorial verification scale tactics native_decide"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6557,"cache_read_input_tokens":36493,"output_tokens":234,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6557},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":234,"cache_read_input_tokens":36493,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6557,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6557,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caox59ZQj7jvGqFhRkJjX","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"f2a19d2c-89a2-4d60-a5cb-7db3ee1afd9a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:42.029Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"01180dee-a7bf-425b-8856-d9d7931c17ae","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"aaa9a46efbbbe9596","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017Ke5ATmDhsnyRxbsnQ3V6d","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"VeriPB CP-SAT OR-Tools proof logging integration support\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A Multi-Stage Proof Logging Framework to Certify the Correctness of CP Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol307-cp2024/LIPIcs.CP.2024.11/LIPIcs.CP.2024.11.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"VeriPB Proof Checking Toolchain\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/veripb-proof-checking-toolchain\"},{\"title\":\"Documentation of VeriPB and CakePB for the SAT Competition 2023 Bart Bogaerts\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2023/downloads/proposals/veripb.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"enable the log of CP-SAT solver · google/or-tools · Discussion #3873\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3873\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding the Log - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html\"},{\"title\":\"Practically feasible proof logging for pseudo-Boolean optimization | Lund University Publications\",\"url\":\"https://lup.lub.lu.se/search/publication/b5de3846-96d8-4689-874a-e0e3f939175c\"},{\"title\":\"Practically Feasible Proof Logging for Pseudo-Boolean Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol340-cp2025/html/LIPIcs.CP.2025.21/LIPIcs.CP.2025.21.html\"},{\"title\":\"VeriPB: The Easy Way to Make Your Combinatorial Search Algorithm Trustworthy\",\"url\":\"https://jakobnordstrom.se/docs/publications/VeriPB_CPTAI2020.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Documentation of VeriPB and CakePB for the SAT Competition 2025 Markus Anders\",\"url\":\"https://jakobnordstrom.se/docs/publications/DocumentationVeriPBandCakePBforSATcompetition2025.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/samples/cp_sat_example.cc at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/samples/cp_sat_example.cc\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding VeriPB, CP-SAT, OR-Tools, and proof logging integration support:\n\n## VeriPB Proof Logging Overview\n\nVeriPB is a proof checking toolchain that constitutes an independent, double-chain framework for certifying the correctness of combinatorial reasoning, especially for high-integrity model checking, pseudo-Boolean (PB) proof logging, and advanced SAT-based optimization.\n\n## Proof Logging for Pseudo-Boolean Optimization\n\nThe research community has developed practical proof logging capabilities. An efficient toolchain based on VeriPB and CakePB for formally verified pseudo-Boolean optimization implements proof logging for the full range of techniques in state-of-the-art solvers RoundingSat and Sat4j, including core-guided search and linear programming integration with Farkas certificates and cut generation, with proof logging and checking performance now quite close to the level of SAT solving.\n\n## CP-SAT and OR-Tools\n\nRegarding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT solver specifically, the search results show discussions about understanding the log of CP-SAT, which shows what the solver is doing and how it is progressing. However, the search results do not indicate that CP-SAT currently has built-in support for VeriPB proof logging integration.\n\n## Constraint Programming Certification Potential\n\nThere is hope that proof logging work could point the way towards practically feasible certified solving for stronger paradigms such as constraint programming and mixed integer programming.\n\nThe search results suggest that while VeriPB is an established tool for proof logging in SAT and pseudo-Boolean solving, direct integration with CP-SAT's proof logging capabilities is not documented in the available sources.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"3379d24e-e4e6-4aaa-95df-a294d6cbe582","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:47.788Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"01180dee-a7bf-425b-8856-d9d7931c17ae","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"58537d00-ea71-4030-9969-a67161f76e29","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"aaa9a46efbbbe9596","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FJK5WVGuXioa79Lj5xrunT","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"proof certificate\" CP-SAT lazy clause generation Pumpkin solver verified\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - ConSol-Lab/Pumpkin: A Lazy Clause Generation Constraint Programming solver written in Rust. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/consol-lab/pumpkin\"},{\"title\":\"Lazy Clause Generation: Combining the Power of SAT and CP (and MIP?) Solving | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-13520-0_3\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Lazy Clause Generation: Combining the power of SAT and CP (and MIP?) solving\",\"url\":\"https://people.eng.unimelb.edu.au/pstuckey/papers/lazy.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Lazy Clause Generation: Combining the Power of SAT and CP (and MIP?) Solving\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/221353593_Lazy_Clause_Generation_Combining_the_Power_of_SAT_and_CP_and_MIP_Solving\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient Verified (UN)SAT Certificate Checking | Journal of Automated Reasoning | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10817-019-09525-z\"},{\"title\":\"A Multi-Stage Proof Logging Framework to Certify the Correctness of CP Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol307-cp2024/LIPIcs.CP.2024.11/LIPIcs.CP.2024.11.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Chuffed, a lazy clause generation solver\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/chuffed/chuffed\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found related to your query:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n### Pumpkin Solver and Proof Certificates\n\nPumpkin is associated with a multi-stage proof logging framework to certify the correctness of CP (Constraint Programming) solvers, published at the 30th International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2024). The proof logging in Pumpkin is defined in the drcp-format component, which can be used in combination with Pumpkin.\n\n### Lazy Clause Generation and CP-SAT\n\nCP-SAT is a portfolio solver centered around a Lazy Clause Generation (LCG) based Constraint Programming Solver. Lazy Clause Generation involves the transformation of the problem into a SAT-formula using a SAT-solver to seek a solution, leveraging an abundance of lazy variables and clauses.\n\n### Verified Proof Checking\n\nThe proof format extends the DRUP format, where nogoods in the proof are RUP clauses which are checked identically to RUP clauses in a DRUP SAT proof, and inferences are temporary problem clauses created by propagators.\n\nThe search results show active research in proof certificate generation and verification for constraint programming solvers, with Pumpkin being a notable lazy clause generation solver that supports proof logging for formal verification of solver correctness.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"55aa3b90-6b76-4a20-9eb4-b3939271c758","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:48.359Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"58537d00-ea71-4030-9969-a67161f76e29","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f2a19d2c-89a2-4d60-a5cb-7db3ee1afd9a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"aaa9a46efbbbe9596","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JbMc9WXc9rTrgHgLenE4J8","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Lean 4 grid placement combinatorial verification scale tactics native_decide\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"decide & native_decide - Decidable Propositions in Lean 4\",\"url\":\"https://lean4.dev/tactics/automation/decide\"},{\"title\":\"rfl Tactic - Prove Reflexivity in Lean 4\",\"url\":\"https://lean4.dev/tactics/core/rfl\"},{\"title\":\"5. Tactics\",\"url\":\"https://lean-lang.org/theorem_proving_in_lean4/Tactics/\"},{\"title\":\"14.5. Tactic Reference\",\"url\":\"https://lean-lang.org/doc/reference/latest/Tactic-Proofs/Tactic-Reference/\"},{\"title\":\"Lean 4 — Learn Functional Programming & Theorem Proving | lean4.dev\",\"url\":\"https://lean4.dev/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - madvorak/lean4-tactics: Overview of tactics in Lean 4 for beginners — longer version\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/madvorak/lean4-tactics\"},{\"title\":\"16. The grind tactic\",\"url\":\"https://lean-lang.org/doc/reference/latest/The--grind--tactic/\"},{\"title\":\"Lean 4: Bridging Formal Mathematics and Software Verification\",\"url\":\"https://leodemoura.github.io/files/CAV2024.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"14.3. The Tactic Language\",\"url\":\"https://lean-lang.org/doc/reference/latest/Tactic-Proofs/The-Tactic-Language/\"},{\"title\":\"6. Tactics — The Lean Reference Manual 3.3.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://leanprover.github.io/reference/tactics.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about Lean 4 tactics related to your query:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**native_decide Tactic:**\nnative_decide uses the native code compiler to evaluate the Decidable instance, which can be significantly more efficient than using reduction, but increases the size of the trusted code base. For better performance with decidable propositions and large computations, use native_decide which compiles to native code.\n\n**decide Tactic:**\nThe decide tactic proves decidable propositions by computation. If Lean can compute whether something is true or false, decide handles it.\n\n**Combinatorial Problems:**\nFor bit-level or pure Boolean combinatorial problems, use bv_decide. The bv_decide tactic calls a state-of-the-art SAT solver (e.g. CaDiCaL or Kissat) and then returns a compact, machine-checkable certificate. The grind tactic is not designed for goals whose search space explodes combinatorially—such as large-n pigeonhole instances, graph-coloring reductions, or high-order N-queens boards.\n\nThe search results don't contain specific information about \"grid placement\" verification or how these tactics scale together in that specific context, but the information above covers the core tactics mentioned in your query.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ce66664b-9e4d-4e25-8e42-e7cca733c3bd","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:48.405Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f2a19d2c-89a2-4d60-a5cb-7db3ee1afd9a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
