{"parentUuid":"adfbc3ef-ab65-4ee4-bd91-a8ed41c27e6a","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aaa9a46efbbbe9596","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01WEm3URTRQ7smu8zi3ZGacz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E37XoHDTXc92eY1GA9e3FY","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"VIPR\" MIP certificate format verifier 2024 2025 large scale"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4163,"cache_read_input_tokens":43050,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4163,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":43,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caox68J2mKjTB3bj76zLS","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"29598251-b0c4-45a7-b0e7-43b89d02a844","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:54.886Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"572c8983-bbd9-4bc7-afb9-c8d15a0f23ac","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"aaa9a46efbbbe9596","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S2Mayg1aZgbZC8jLUM5k3Z","type":"tool_result","content":"# AlphaProof: Capabilities, Limitations, and Scope\n\n## Key Capabilities\n\nAlphaProof demonstrated remarkable success on high-difficulty mathematics, achieving \"silver medal performance\" by solving three of six International Mathematical Olympiad 2024 problems, including P6—which only 5 of 609 human competitors fully solved.\n\nThe system excels at producing \"outputs in formal language that can be verified automatically,\" eliminating hallucination concerns present in natural language models. It also demonstrates \"scalability of test-time compute to obtain improved answers over many orders of magnitude.\"\n\n## Stated Limitations\n\nThe article provides **no information** about applications beyond formal mathematical proofs. There is no discussion of combinatorial optimization, NP-hard problems, or domains outside theorem-proving in Lean.\n\nRegarding proof scale, the document indicates proofs consist of \"tens to hundreds of tactics\" but provides no explicit maximum complexity metrics or comparative analysis against human-written proofs of varying lengths.\n\n## Future Scope\n\nThe author notes this is \"just the beginning\" with \"many ideas for how we can make AlphaProof better as well as more general,\" but doesn't specify what those domains might be. The technical approach appears specialized to Lean's formal proof system rather than general optimization problems.\n\n**In summary:** The blog post focuses exclusively on mathematical theorem-proving capabilities without addressing broader applications or detailed scaling limitations."}]},"uuid":"15c67972-1762-41be-8680-79436e9cc18e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:00.608Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"572c8983-bbd9-4bc7-afb9-c8d15a0f23ac","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"adfbc3ef-ab65-4ee4-bd91-a8ed41c27e6a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"aaa9a46efbbbe9596","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GSwJqSb3doExpWDHsu9zpM","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Isabelle HOL Coq combinatorial optimization solver verification industrial application 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"[1808.09701] Comparison of Two Theorem Provers: Isabelle/HOL and Coq\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1808.09701\"},{\"title\":\"Comparison of Two Theorem Provers: Isabelle/HOL and Coq\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1808.09701\"},{\"title\":\"Welcome to a World of Rocq\",\"url\":\"https://rocq-prover.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Automating Interactive Theorem Provers and Certifying Automatic Theorem Provers\",\"url\":\"https://homepage.divms.uiowa.edu/~viswanathn/compmain.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Tobias Nipkow Lawrence C. Paulson Markus Wenzel λ → ∀ = Isabelle β α HOL\",\"url\":\"https://isabelle.in.tum.de/doc/tutorial.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Isabelle/HOL: a proof assistant for higher-order logic | Guide books | ACM Digital Library\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.5555/1791547\"},{\"title\":\"Isabelle (proof assistant) - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isabelle_(proof_assistant)\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction to the Coq proof-assistant for practical software veriﬁcation\",\"url\":\"https://www.lri.fr/~paulin/LASER/course-notes.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Lightweight Program Construction and Verification Tools in Isabelle/HOL\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/264859276_Lightweight_Program_Construction_and_Verification_Tools_in_IsabelleHOL\"},{\"title\":\"From Zero to QED: An informal introduction to formality in Lean 4\",\"url\":\"https://sdiehl.github.io/zero-to-qed/03_theorem_provers.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about Isabelle/HOL and Coq theorem provers and their applications, though the results don't contain specific information about a 2025 industrial application combining all these elements specifically.\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**General Information on Theorem Provers:**\nBoth Isabelle/HOL and Coq can be used to solve complex engineering problems, such as proving security properties of software systems or algorithms.\n\n**Industrial Applications:**\nCoq had CompCert and Isabelle had seL4 as major industrial-scale verification projects that demonstrated the practical viability of these tools.\n\n**Verification Capabilities:**\nResearch includes verification of algorithms like closest pair of points algorithms and a solver for linear mixed integer arithmetic in Isabelle/HOL. Additionally, work has been done combining SAT solvers with computer algebra systems to verify combinatorial conjectures.\n\n**Program Verification and Extraction:**\nRocq (formerly Coq) is an interactive theorem prover designed to develop mathematical proofs and write formal specifications, with the additional feature of automatically extracting executable programs from specifications as OCaml or Haskell source code.\n\nHowever, the search results do not contain specific information about a 2025 industrial application that specifically combines Isabelle/HOL, Coq, and combinatorial optimization solvers. The results show historical applications and general capabilities of these tools, but not a specific 2025 project matching all the criteria in your query.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b4494155-ca30-4727-ae49-8d4589c41a8f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:00.837Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"adfbc3ef-ab65-4ee4-bd91-a8ed41c27e6a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"29598251-b0c4-45a7-b0e7-43b89d02a844","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"aaa9a46efbbbe9596","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E37XoHDTXc92eY1GA9e3FY","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"VIPR\" MIP certificate format verifier 2024 2025 large scale\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Satisfiability Modulo Theories for Verifying MILP Certificates\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2312.10420\"},{\"title\":\"Certifying MIP-Based Presolve Reductions for 0–1 Integer Linear Programs\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2401.09277\"},{\"title\":\"[2312.10420] Satisfiability Modulo Theories for Verifying MILP Certificates\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.10420\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding VIPR – Virtual Incident Procurement (2025 Update) - Govology\",\"url\":\"https://govology.com/product/understanding-vipr-virtual-incident-procurement/\"},{\"title\":\"Incident Procurement - Virtual Incident PRocurement (VIPR Next Gen) - vipr\",\"url\":\"https://www.fs.usda.gov/business/incident/vipr.php\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Verified-Intelligence/alpha-beta-CROWN: alpha-beta-CROWN: An Efficient, Scalable and GPU Accelerated Neural Network Verifier (winner of VNN-COMP 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025) · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Verified-Intelligence/alpha-beta-CROWN\"},{\"title\":\"Jan. 2025: Become a Wildland Firefighting Vendor - Norcal APEX Accelerator\",\"url\":\"https://www.apexnorcal.org/webinar/jan-2025-become-a-wildland-firefighting-vendor/\"},{\"title\":\"ViPR 3.5.0.0 Support Matrix - REV 20c | PDF | Hyper V | Operating System Technology\",\"url\":\"https://www.scribd.com/document/339279235/ViPR-3-5-0-0-Support-Matrix-REV-20c\"},{\"title\":\"platelogiq 2024 price list vipr vehicle intelligence and plate ...\",\"url\":\"https://ucnj.org/vendor-opportunities/wp-content/uploads/sites/9/2025/06/Platelogic-VIPR-2024-Price-List-MSRP.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"VIPR 2025 IBPA Clerical Support Unit Region 13 National Zone\",\"url\":\"https://www.highergov.com/contract-opportunity/request-for-information-vipr-2025-ibpa-clerical-s-f88ba/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about VIPR related to Mixed Integer Linear Programming (MILP):\n\nVIPR 1.0 is the first recently proposed general certificate format for answers produced by MILP solvers. VIPR 1.0 is a branch-and-cut general certificate format for MILP instances which handles optimality, infeasibility, and relaxed optimality bounds.\n\nVIPR 1.0 is designed with simplicity in mind, and is composed of a list of statements that can be sequentially verified using a limited number of inference rules.\n\nRegarding verification approaches, recent research has developed enhanced verification methods for VIPR certificates. A schema encodes VIPR's inference rules as a ground formula that completely characterizes the validity of the algorithmic check, and implements a checker for VIPR certificates by expressing this formula with the Satisfiability Modulo Theory Library (SMT-LIB).\n\nThe VIPR format implementation is currently integrated into solvers: VIPR 1.0 is currently implemented in the latest versions of exact SCIP, together with a checker (viprchk implemented in C++) for the corresponding certificates.\n\nThis research appears in academic papers from 2024-2025, addressing large-scale verification of MILP certificate formats.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"60cc0b07-16b1-43c5-b13c-2b43e13cdc56","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:01.094Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"29598251-b0c4-45a7-b0e7-43b89d02a844","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
