{"parentUuid":"bbf259ff-a5d8-4fff-87be-f2f026fae794","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"aaa9a46efbbbe9596","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FeKpsWMNv9rS4Nv549MBJf","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"AlphaProof\" combinatorics weakness limitation problem class scope 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"AlphaProof Paper\",\"url\":\"https://www.julian.ac/blog/2025/11/13/alphaproof-paper/\"},{\"title\":\"AI achieves silver-medal standard solving International Mathematical Olympiad problems — Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/blog/ai-solves-imo-problems-at-silver-medal-level/\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaProof When RL meets Formal Maths Thomas HUBERT, March 2025\",\"url\":\"https://rdi.berkeley.edu/adv-llm-agents/slides/alphaproof.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Olympiad-level formal mathematical reasoning with reinforcement learning | Nature\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-09833-y\"},{\"title\":\"AI's Mathematical Milestone: Solving Olympiad Problems - Gradient Flow\",\"url\":\"https://gradientflow.com/alphaproof-alphageometry-2/\"},{\"title\":\"The 2025 International Mathematical Olympiad | rishimehta.xyz\",\"url\":\"https://rishimehta.xyz/2025/08/09/imo-2025-results.html\"},{\"title\":\"When AI Meets Formal Maths: The Story of AlphaProof\",\"url\":\"https://kargichauhan.github.io/kargisnotebook.github.io/posts/AlphaProof.html\"},{\"title\":\"Google latest models prove AI doesn't have to suck at math • The Register\",\"url\":\"https://www.theregister.com/2024/07/26/google_deepmind_maths/\"},{\"title\":\"What will the IMO tell us about AI math capabilities? | Epoch AI\",\"url\":\"https://epoch.ai/gradient-updates/what-will-the-imo-tell-us-about-ai-math-capabilities/\"},{\"title\":\"An AI system could win a medal at the International Mathematical Olympiad, according to a study\",\"url\":\"https://sciencemediacentre.es/en/ai-system-could-win-medal-international-mathematical-olympiad-according-study\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found regarding AlphaProof's weakness in combinatorics:\n\n## Combinatorics as a Key Limitation\n\nAlphaProof solved two algebra problems and one number theory problem, while the two combinatorics problems remained unsolved. This represents a significant gap in the system's capabilities.\n\n### Performance Data\n\nOn formal-imo, TTRL reached particularly strong performance in number theory (75.7%) and algebra (72.6%), and also made progress in combinatorics (20.3%). This shows combinatorics performance is substantially lower than other mathematical domains.\n\n### Root Cause and Context\n\nThe results show strengths in certain areas (algebra, geometry) and weaknesses in others (combinatorics), aligning with the previous article's point about varying ease of encoding different mathematical fields. This was despite it being an unlucky topic distribution relative to the system's strengths. The system was weakest at combinatorics, and the two problems AlphaProof didn't solve (P3 and P5) were combinatorics problems.\n\n### Scope and Problem Class\n\nThe specific problems where AlphaProof struggled were the two combinatorics problems posed in the 2024 IMO competition. The limitation suggests that certain combinatorial problem structures pose particular challenges to the system's proof-search methodology, though the exact nature of these challenges in terms of problem structure or formalization difficulty isn't fully detailed in the available sources.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e627aba6-8930-4c2b-8178-c4aa24d33cb0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:11.632Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bbf259ff-a5d8-4fff-87be-f2f026fae794","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"300331aa-76f6-49e9-820f-2ff7c728e758","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"aaa9a46efbbbe9596","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EAmAt9fuFNAXJFf7kVN7qe","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"reflection\" Lean tactic large search space verification scaling memory\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Small Scale Reflection for the Working Lean User Vladimir Gladshtein # Ñ\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2403.12733\"},{\"title\":\"Lean Tips and Tricks\",\"url\":\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/lean3/tips_and_tricks.html\"},{\"title\":\"Leanabell-Prover: Posttraining Scaling in Formal Reasoning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2504.06122v1\"},{\"title\":\"lean-smt: An SMT Tactic for Discharging Proof Goals in Lean | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-98682-6_11\"},{\"title\":\"[2403.12733] Small Scale Reflection for the Working Lean User\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.12733\"},{\"title\":\"Aristotle: IMO-level Automated Theorem Proving The Harmonic Team Abstract\",\"url\":\"https://harmonic.fun/pdf/Aristotle_IMO_Level_Automated_Theorem_Proving.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Lean 4: Formal Theorems\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/formal-lean-4-theorems\"},{\"title\":\"Scaling Test-time Compute for LLM Agents\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2506.12928\"},{\"title\":\"Solving Formal Math Problems by Decomposition and Iterative Reflection\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2507.15225v1\"},{\"title\":\"Lean Benchmarks in Systems & Theorem Proving\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/lean-benchmarks\"}]\n\nI found search results related to your query about reflection, Lean tactics, large search spaces, verification, scaling, and memory. Here's a summary of the relevant findings:\n\n## Key Results:\n\n**Small Scale Reflection in Lean 4:**\nThe Small Scale Reflection (SSR) proof methodology and tactic language has been implemented for the Lean 4 proof assistant. LeanSSR provides powerful rewriting principles and means for effective management of hypotheses in the proof context, similar to its Coq predecessor SSReflect.\n\n**Computational Reflection for Decision Procedures:**\nFor proof rules involving complex side conditions or computations such as arithmetic simplifications, reflection can be encoded into a reflective decision procedure, which can be formally verified in Lean.\n\n**Memory and Resource Management in Large Search Spaces:**\nLean has two configurable flags for configuring its resource usage—memory and execution time—and when writing proofs it can be helpful to increase these options if deterministic timeouts or out of memory issues slow down development. This is especially helpful when using tactics like library_search, which may run for a long time but then produce a result that tells us a much faster tactic to use if they succeed.\n\n**Scaling in Formal Verification:**\nRecent work uncovers log-linear trends between proof length, CPU usage, and solved problem count, which provide quantitative insight into the scaling properties of Lean-based automated theorem proving.\n\nThe search results show that reflection techniques in Lean are used both for concise proof structuring and for decision procedures, while memory and execution time constraints are critical considerations when dealing with large search spaces in formal verification.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"418b9f8d-ddd9-40e0-a534-1b69159a8f8c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:13.243Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"300331aa-76f6-49e9-820f-2ff7c728e758","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"418b9f8d-ddd9-40e0-a534-1b69159a8f8c","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aaa9a46efbbbe9596","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013eipuAVzJRV8iArFVF2nNA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have plenty of solid evidence. Let me synthesize this into the user's required output format.\n\n---\n\n# Lean 4 / AlphaProof 在组合优化最优性证明上的深度调研\n\n## 一、AlphaProof 现状（截至 2026.05）：组合优化是它最弱的领域\n\nAlphaProof 论文 2025 年 11 月正式发表在 Nature 上（Nature 645）。关键事实：\n\n- **它就是为 IMO 类纯数学定理设计的**，靠 RL+test-time RL 在 Lean 4 里搜证明，没有任何向组合优化扩展的迹象。\n- **2024 IMO 它没解出来的两题恰恰是组合学（P3、P5）**。formal-IMO 基准上分领域命中率：number theory 75.7%、algebra 72.6%、**combinatorics 仅 20.3%**。这是公开数据里 AlphaProof 最大的短板。\n- **没有任何后续工作把它推向 NP-hard 实例的最优性证明**。DeepMind 的\"组合优化\"线放在了 **AlphaEvolve**（2025.05 发布，arXiv 2506.13131），那是用 LLM+进化框架去发现/改进算法（MAX-4-CUT、矩阵乘法、调度启发式），**不输出 Lean 证明**，跟形式化不在一个赛道。\n- **AlphaProof 与 AlphaEvolve 是两条独立产品线**，前者形式化数学，后者算法/启发式发现，没有交叉。\n\n**结论 1：把 AlphaProof 套到我们 70×70 + 266 设施\"这个 placement 是最优\"的诉求上，没有现成路径，且其最弱项正是组合学。**\n\n## 二、Lean 4 在组合优化最优性证明的实际进展\n\n近一年最重要的工作是 **PBLean**（arXiv 2602.08692，2026 年初）：\n\n- 把 **VeriPB pseudo-Boolean 证明证书**导入 Lean 4，靠 `native_decide` 反射式 checker（同 `bv_decide` 模式），soundness 在 Lean 里证。\n- **规模实测**：Paley graph 独立数 Paley(101)，约 6.3 万行证书，3.5 分钟通过；显式 proof term 在 p≥37 就超 60s 爆掉。\n- 关键意义：**它不是让 Lean 自己去搜最优性证明**，而是让外部 PB solver 出证书、Lean 只做 checker。这跟 AlphaProof \"让 AI 写 Lean tactic\" 是相反的范式。\n\n其他相关：\n- **LeanSAT**（leanprover/leansat）：UNSAT LRAT 证书的 Lean checker，覆盖 CaDiCaL 输出，但只到 SAT，不到 PB。\n- **bv_decide tactic**：对 bit-vector 类组合走 SAT+LRAT，是 Lean 4 内置最接近\"组合优化决策\"的工具。\n- **lean-smt**（Springer 2025）：把 Lean goal 丢给 SMT 求解，但不是优化。\n\n**Lean 直接形式化\"70×70 grid + 266 设施 placement 最优\"这件事没人做过**，工程上要做：\n1. 定义 grid、设施、占用、合法 placement、目标函数 `max_lex(area, min_side)` —— 这一层 Lean 写得出来，但纯 boring；\n2. 证\"不存在更大的 ghost 矩形\" —— 这是状态空间爆炸点。直接 `decide`/`native_decide` 70×70 是天文数字；只有走\"外部求解器出 PB 证书 + PBLean 验\"这条路才可行。\n\n## 三、对比：Lean 路线 vs VeriPB+CakePB 路线\n\n| 维度 | Lean 4 直接形式化 | VeriPB + CakePB（PB 路线）|\n|---|---|---|\n| Trust base | Lean kernel | CakeML 编译出的二进制 + HOL4 kernel |\n| Solver 集成 | 几乎没有现成工程 | RoundingSat、Sat4j 都已支持 PB 证书；**CP-SAT 不支持** |\n| 规模 | Paley(101) 6 万行已属高水位 | SAT/PB 竞赛级，已是工业级（每年 SAT Comp 强制双 checker 验所有结果） |\n| LLM 协作 | APOLLO、DeepSeek-Prover-V2（671B，miniF2F 88.9%）、LeanCopilot 都成熟 | 不需要 LLM，纯证书校验 |\n| 工程成本 | 高，要写大量定义和 spec | 低，证书是 solver 旁路输出 |\n\n**CP-SAT 是关键卡点**：OR-Tools CP-SAT 至今**没有 VeriPB 输出能力**（CP 2024 多阶段证明日志框架是给 Pumpkin 这种 LCG-CP 用的，CP-SAT 工程上没接）。所以即便我们走 PB 路线，也得先做 **CP-SAT → PB 证书**的 lift，或者换 solver（Pumpkin、exact-SCIP）。exact-SCIP 已实现 VIPR 1.0 MIP 证书（arXiv 2401.09277），是目前最现成的 MIP 优化证书工具链。\n\n## 四、LLM 帮写 Lean 证明：能力边界\n\n- APOLLO（arXiv 2505.05758）miniF2F 84.9%（<8B 模型）；DeepSeek-Prover-V2-671B 88.9%、PutnamBench 49/658；Goedel-Prover、Llemma 都开放可用。\n- 但这些都是 **olympiad/undergrad 级数学**，**不是工业组合优化最优性**。\n- Claude/GPT 让 AI agent 直接给 70×70 placement 写 Lean 证明，**目前没有可信路径**。能做的是：让 LLM 写定义层（schema、约束规范），证书层走 PBLean。\n\n## 五、对我们 PROJECT_LOCK / Phase 5 的判断\n\n**坚持 VeriPB+CakePB / VIPR 路线，不要押注 Lean 直接形式化。**\n\n理由：\n1. **AlphaProof 在组合学只有 20.3%**，把它当 NP-hard 最优性证明工具是误用。\n2. PBLean 已经把 PB→Lean 的桥搭好；如果未来想升级 trust base，用\"VeriPB 证书 + PBLean 反射 checker\" 比\"重写整个 Lean 形式化\"省 10 倍工。\n3. **真正阻塞我们的是 CP-SAT 不出证书**，不是缺 Lean。Phase 5 的第一步该是：评估 (a) CP-SAT 加 PB 证书 patch 的可行性，或 (b) 切到能出证书的 solver（exact-SCIP / Pumpkin）做最终 ratification 通道。\n4. **Phase 5 stretch goal 重排**：先做 VIPR/PB 证书层 → 再加 CakePB 二进制校验 → 最后才考虑 PBLean 把语义提升到 Lean 命题（\"this placement is optimal w.r.t. spec X\"）。AlphaProof / LLM-写-Lean-tactic 留作\"远期演示性\"任务，不进核心路径。\n5. **AI agent 在我们项目的合理位置仍然是 sidecar**（与 PROJECT_LOCK 的 AI Safety Contract 一致），不该让 Claude/GPT 写 Lean 证明当作 trust source。\n\n**建议布局节奏**：\n- 短期（Phase 3B-4）：保持 OR-Tools CP-SAT 信任 + 自检 + AI shadow，不动证书层；\n- 中期（Phase 5.A）：试点 exact-SCIP 跑同问题作为 cross-check，输出 VIPR 证书 + viprchk 校验；\n- 长期（Phase 5.B / stretch）：如果工业界 PB-CP 证书工具链成熟（Pumpkin + drcp-format 已上路），引入 PBLean 把 ghost 矩形最优性提升到 Lean 命题层；\n- **不建议**投资 AlphaProof / LLM 写 tactic 路线，时机未到、领域不匹配。\n\n## 关键文献清单\n\n- AlphaProof, Nature 2025: https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-09833-y\n- PBLean (arXiv 2602.08692): https://arxiv.org/html/2602.08692v1\n- VeriPB+CakePB SAT Comp 2025: https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/downloads/checkers/veripb.pdf\n- Practically Feasible PB Optimization Proof Logging (CP 2025): https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.21\n- Multi-Stage CP Proof Logging (CP 2024): https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol307-cp2024/LIPIcs.CP.2024.11/LIPIcs.CP.2024.11.pdf\n- VIPR / exact-SCIP MILP 证书 (arXiv 2401.09277): https://arxiv.org/pdf/2401.09277\n- AlphaEvolve (arXiv 2506.13131): https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.13131\n- APOLLO (arXiv 2505.05758): https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.05758\n- DeepSeek-Prover-V2 (arXiv 2504.21801): https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.21801\n- cake_lpr / CakeML: https://cakeml.org/checkers.html\n- Pumpkin LCG-CP solver: https://github.com/consol-lab/pumpkin"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2708,"cache_read_input_tokens":50664,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2708,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caox7xUF6to6qUvYvdBmY","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"f877abf0-c20f-41b2-b7d2-06db58632779","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:54:20.305Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
